      "message": "Not new to this CL, but I suspect there are other cases where this falls apart: we\u0027re copying `width` bytes per row, which assumes 8 bits/pixel.  But that\u0027s not true for all formats, e.g. `kBW_Format`.  So if we can reach this with a non-8bpp format, we\u0027re blown.\n\nI think it\u0027s reachable when 1) `filterMask` returns false, and 2) we\u0027re dealing with a non-deterministic font which changes the reported bounds between loads.\n\n(Historically, this seems to have been introduced in https://skia-review.git.corp.google.com/c/skia/+/392156: previously, the memcpy loop was guarded by filtermask succeeding, which guarantees an 8bpp format.)\n\nMight be interesting to sick Gemini on producing a repro for something like that.  I\u0027ll leave it up to you if you want to pursue here or in a follow up.",
